.TH KNOTS 1 "2026-06-22" "knots 1.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
knots \- C/C++ code complexity analyzer with AI cost metrics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B knots
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.br
.B knots
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB\-\-compile\-commands\fR <\fIFILE\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B knots
is a fast C/C++ code complexity analyzer built on tree-sitter.
It measures traditional complexity metrics alongside two AI-specific cost scores \(em
.B AIRD
(AI Reasoning Difficulty) and
.B AICP
(AI Context Pressure) \(em to identify which functions are genuinely expensive to
modify with AI assistance.
.PP
.B knots
computes the following metrics for each function:
.TP
.B McCabe Cyclomatic Complexity
Counts decision points (if, while, for, do, switch, ternary, logical operators).
Validated to match pmccabe output exactly.
.TP
.B Cognitive Complexity
Measures difficulty to understand code, emphasizing nesting and structural
complexity.
Based on the SonarSource specification.
.TP
.B Nesting Depth
Maximum nesting level of control structures.
.TP
.B SLOC
Source lines of code (non-blank, non-comment).
.TP
.B ABC Complexity
Assignment, Branch, Condition magnitude: sqrt(A\(S2 + B\(S2 + C\(S2).
.TP
.B Return Count
Number of return statements in a function.
.TP
.B Test Scoring
Multi-dimensional test difficulty metric across signature, dependency,
observable, implementation, and documentation axes.
.TP
.B External Calls
Count of unique identifier-form call targets not defined in the same translation
unit. Measures external dependency breadth (out-of-file functions and
function-like macros).
.TP
.B AIRD \(em AI Reasoning Difficulty
Normalized 0\(en100 score predicting how much reasoning effort an AI model needs
to safely modify a function.
Formula: (cognitive/75 \(mu 55) + (sloc/200 \(mu 15) + (nesting/8 \(mu 15) +
(test_score/20 \(mu 15) \(mi (doc_score/10 \(mu 15).
Corpus-validated; recommended CI threshold: 85.
.TP
.B AICP \(em AI Context Pressure
Normalized 0\(en100 score predicting how much context an AI model must load before
it can act. Complements AIRD: a function can be cheap to load but hard to reason
about, or expensive to load but trivial once context is assembled.
Formula: (external_calls/20 \(mu 60) + (sloc/200 \(mu 40) \(mi (doc_score/10 \(mu 15).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Recursively process all C/C++ source files in directories.
When used, a
.I report.txt
file is generated with per-function details.
Header files (.h, .hpp, .hxx) are skipped by default.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show detailed per-function analysis.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-matrix
Show testability matrix categorization.
Functions are placed into four quadrants:
QUICK WINS (low complexity, easy to test),
INVEST IN TESTS (high complexity, easy to test),
ADD DOCS (low complexity, hard to test),
REFACTOR (high complexity, hard to test).
.TP
.BI \-\-compile\-commands " FILE"
Use a
.I compile_commands.json
file (from CMake, Bear, etc.) to get the list of files to analyze.
Mutually exclusive with the positional \fIFILE\fR argument.
.TP
.BI \-\-include " FILE"
Include filter rules from a JSON file (whitelist).
See
.BR FILTERS
below.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " FILE"
Exclude filter rules from a JSON file (blacklist).
See
.BR FILTERS
below.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
Output format. One of:
.RS
.TP
.B text
Human-readable output (default).
.TP
.B sarif
SARIF 2.1.0 JSON for VS Code / GitHub Code Scanning.
.TP
.B json
JSON array of per-function metrics.
.TP
.B ndjson
Newline-delimited JSON \(em one record per line, composable via find/xargs.
.TP
.B csv
CSV with header row.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-mccabe\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this McCabe complexity.
.TP
.BI \-\-cognitive\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this cognitive complexity.
.TP
.BI \-\-nesting\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this nesting depth.
.TP
.BI \-\-sloc\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this SLOC count.
.TP
.BI \-\-abc\-threshold " F"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this ABC magnitude.
.TP
.BI \-\-return\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this return count.
.TP
.BI \-\-aird\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this AIRD score.
Recommended value: 85 (empirically validated against Sonnet 4.6 and Opus 4.8).
.TP
.BI \-\-aicp\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this AICP score.
.TP
.BI \-\-external\-calls\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this external call count.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help message.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information.
.SH FILTERS
Filter rules are specified in JSON files with the following optional fields:
.TP
.B file_patterns
Glob patterns for file paths.
Supports \fB*\fR, \fB**\fR, and \fB!\fR for negation.
.TP
.B function_patterns
Regular expression patterns for function names.
.TP
.B min_complexity
Minimum complexity threshold (inclusive).
.TP
.B max_complexity
Maximum complexity threshold (inclusive).
.PP
Example filter file:
.RS
.nf
{
    "file_patterns": ["src/**/*.c"],
    "function_patterns": ["^handle_"],
    "min_complexity": 10
}
.fi
.RE
.SH COMPLEXITY INDICATORS
.B knots
uses visual emoji indicators based on the maximum of McCabe and
Cognitive complexity:
.PP
.RS
.nf
1\-10   Good     \- Low complexity, easy to maintain
11\-20  Okay     \- Moderate complexity, may need attention
21\-49  Bad      \- High complexity, consider refactoring
50+    Critical \- Very high complexity, refactor immediately
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful analysis, no threshold violations.
.TP
.B 1
Error occurred (file not found, parse error, invalid arguments), or one or more
threshold violations were detected (when any \fB\-\-*\-threshold\fR flag is set).
.SH EXAMPLES
Analyze a single file:
.RS
.nf
knots path/to/file.c
.fi
.RE
.PP
Recursively analyze a directory:
.RS
.nf
knots \-r path/to/project/
.fi
.RE
.PP
CI gate \(em fail if any function has AIRD > 85:
.RS
.nf
knots \-r src/ \-\-aird\-threshold 85
.fi
.RE
.PP
Corpus analysis \(em one JSON record per function, composable across files:
.RS
.nf
find . \-name "*.c" | xargs knots \-\-format ndjson > metrics.ndjson
.fi
.RE
.PP
Filter high-AIRD functions via jq:
.RS
.nf
find src/ \-name "*.c" | xargs knots \-\-format ndjson | jq 'select(.aird > 70)'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Analyze files from a compilation database:
.RS
.nf
knots \-\-compile\-commands build/compile_commands.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
SARIF output for GitHub Code Scanning:
.RS
.nf
knots \-r \-\-format sarif src/ > knots.sarif
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I report.txt
Generated in the current directory when using \fB\-r\fR mode.
Contains per-function complexity details.
.TP
.I compile_commands.json
Compilation database used with \fB\-\-compile\-commands\fR.
